cepts module-not-found errors and suggests similar modules.", records={{fields={{"install", "function()", ""}, {"uninstall", "function()", ""}, {"module_exists", "function(name: string): boolean", ""}, {"format_error", "function(name: string): string", ""}}, line=208, name="RequireModule"}}}, ["cosmic.sandbox"]={examples={}, file="lib/cosmic/sandbox.tl", functions={{description=" Restricts system calls available to the process.\n Pledging causes most system calls to become unavailable. Using pledge is irreversible.\n On Linux disabled calls return EPERM; OpenBSD kills the process.\n Common promise groups include:\n - \"stdio\": Standard I/O operations (read, write, close, etc.)\n - \"rpath\": Read-only path operations\n - \"wpath\": Write operations on paths\n - \"cpath\": Create/remove paths\n - \"flock\": File locking operations\n - \"tty\": Terminal operations (isatty, tiocgwinsz, etc.)\n - \"inet\": IPv4/IPv6 socket operations\n - \"unix\": UNIX domain sockets\n - \"proc\": fork, vfork, kill, wait, etc.\n - \"exec\": execve operations\n - \"unveil\": Allow unveil() calls", is_local=true, line=26, name="pledge", params={{description="Space-separated promise groups (nil = unrestricted)", name="promises", param_type="string|nil"}, {description="Promises for child processes after exec (nil = unrestricted)", name="execpromises", param_type="string|nil"}, {description="Optional mode flags", name="mode", param_type="number|nil"}}, returns={{description="True on success", return_type="boolean"}}, signature="(promises?: string, execpromises?: string, mode?: number): boolean"}, {description=" Restricts filesystem visibility to specified paths.\n Once you start using unveil, the entire filesystem is hidden.\n You then specify which paths should become visible by repeatedly calling unveil.\n When finished, call unveil(nil, nil) to commit and lock the policy.\n Permissions:\n - \"r\": Read-only path operations (corresponds to pledge \"rpath\")\n - \"w\": Write operations (corresponds to pledge \"wpath\")\n - \"x\": Execute operations (corresponds to pledge \"exec\"/\"execnative\")\n - \"c\": Create and remove paths (corresponds to pledge \"cpath\")", is_local=true, line=44, name="unveil", params={{description="Path to unveil (nil to commit policy)", name="path", param_type="string|nil"}, {description="Permission string like \"r\", \"rw\", \"rwxc\" (nil to commit)", name="permissions", param_type="string|nil"}}, returns={{description="True on success", return_type="boolean"}}, signature="(path: string, permissions: string): boolean"}}, module_doc=" Security sandboxing utilities.\n Wraps cosmo.unix for pledge and unveil operations to restrict system calls and filesystem access.", records={{fields={{"pledge", "function(promises?: string, execpromises?: string, mode?: number): boolean", ""}, {"unveil", "function(path: string, permissions: string): boolean", ""}}, line=48, name="SandboxModule"}}}, ["cosmic.shm"]={examples={}, file="lib/cosmic/shm.tl", functions={{description=" Creates a shared memory region.\n The memory is shared across fork() and can be used for inter-process\n communication with atomic operations and futex synchronization.\n Example usage for a simple mutex:\n ```lua\n local shm = require(\"cosmic.shm\")\n local mem = shm.mapshared(8000 * 8)\n local LOCK = 0  -- word index for lock\n -- Lock acquisition\n while mem:xchg(LOCK, 1) == 1 do\n   mem:wait(LOCK, 1)\n end\n -- Critical section here\n -- Unlock\n mem:store(LOCK, 0)\n mem:wake(LOCK, 1)\n ```", is_local=true, line=66, name="mapshared", params={{description="Size in bytes for the shared memory region", name="size", param_type="number"}}, returns={{description="Shared memory object with atomic operations", return_type="Memory"}}, signature="(size: number): ShmModule.Memory"}}, module_doc=" Shared memory for inter-process communication.\n Provides atomic operations and wait/wake primitives for synchronization.\n Memory created with mapshared is shared across fork() and provides\n fundamental synchronization primitives including futexes.", records={{description=" Module type for shared memory operations.", fields={{"Methods", "", " Memory record type for shared memory operations.\n Memory encapsulates shared memory with atomic operations."}, {"read", "function(self: Memory, offset?: number, bytes?: number): string", ""}, {"write", "function(self: Memory, data: string, offset?: number, bytes?: number)", ""}, {"load", "function(self: Memory, word_index: number): number", ""}, {"store", "function(self: Memory, word_index: number, value: number)", ""}, {"xchg", "function(self: Memory, word_index: number, value: number): number", ""}, {"cmpxchg", "function(self: Memory, word_index: number, old: number, new: number): boolean, number", ""}, {"fetch_add", "function(self: Memory, word_index: number, value: number): number", ""}, {"fetch_and", "function(self: Memory, word_index: number, value: number): number", ""}, {"fetch_or", "function(self: Memory, word_index: number, value: number): number", ""}, {"fetch_xor", "function(self: Memory, word_index: number, value: number): number", ""}, {"wait", "function(self: Memory, word_index: number, expect: number, abs_deadline?: number, nanos?: number): number", ""}, {"wake", "function(self: Memory, word_index: number, count?: number): number", ""}, {"mapshared", "function(size: number): Memory", ""}, {"mutex", "", " Creates a shared memory region.\n The memory is shared across fork() and can be used for inter-process\n communication with atomic operations and futex synchronization."}, {"mem", "xchg(LOCK, 1) == 1 do", " Creates a shared memory region.\n The memory is shared across fork() and can be used for inter-process\n communication with atomic operations and futex synchronization.\n Example usage for a simple mutex:\n ```lua\n local shm = require(\"cosmic.shm\")\n local mem = shm.mapshared(8000 * 8)\n local LOCK = 0  -- word index for lock\n -- Lock acquisition"}, {"mem", "wait(LOCK, 1)", " Cr